  Sitting up, I accept the stainless steel cup. It is cold to the touch, reminding me that winter is here.

//　一口に飲み干すと、金属臭混じりの水道水は世辞に
//も美味とは言えなかったが、それでも心地良く胃の腑
//の底へ染み渡った。
//　大きく息をつく。
  I gulp it down. Tap water, the metallic tang tells me, but its cool kiss upon my organs more than makes up for what it lacks in flavor.

//　その途端、腹が鳴った。
